[38;2;124;124;124mthere exists a neighborhood U of x such that the restriction of F to U is zero.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThis is a standard result. Let me think carefully.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe support of a coherent sheaf F on a noetherian scheme is closed. Actually, [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mthe support Supp(F) = {x ∈ X : F_x ≠ 0} is a closed subset when F is coherent [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mand X is noetherian (more generally, F of finite type over a locally noetherian [0m[38;2;124;124;124mscheme, or F of finite presentation).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mActually let me recall: For a coherent sheaf F on a locally noetherian scheme, [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mSupp(F) is closed. The proof: locally, F is the cokernel of O^m → O^n, and the [0m
[38;2;124;124;124msupport is where the cokernel is nonzero, which is the closed set defined by the[0m[38;2;124;124;124mfitting ideal / the annihilator.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo if F_x = 0, then x ∉ Supp(F), and since Supp(F) is closed, its complement is [0m[38;2;124;124;124man open neighborhood U of x with F|_U = 0.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo the statement is TRUE.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me write a complete proof.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mProof: It suffices to show that the support Supp(F) = {y ∈ X : F_y ≠ 0} is a [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mclosed subset of X. Then if F_x = 0, x is in the open complement X \ Supp(F), [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mwhich is an open neighborhood U of x with F|_U = 0.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mTo show Supp(F) is closed: Cover X by affine open noetherian schemes Spec A_i. [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mOn each Spec A_i, F|_{Spec A_i} = M_i~ for a finitely generated A_i-module M_i [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(coherent = finite type on locally noetherian). The support of M_i~ in Spec A_i [0m[38;2;124;124;124mis V(Ann(M_i)), which is closed. Indeed, for p ∈ Spec A_i, (M_i~)_p = (M_i)_p, [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mand (M_i)_p = 0 iff there exists s ∉ p with sM_i = 0, iff Ann(M_i) ⊄ p, iff p ∉ [0m[38;2;124;124;124mV(Ann(M_i)). So Supp(M_i~) = V(Ann(M_i)) is closed in Spec A_i. Since the [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mSupp(F) ∩ Spec A_i = Supp(F|_{Spec A_i}) = V(Ann(M_i)) is closed in Spec A_i for[0m[38;2;124;124;124meach i, and these glue, Supp(F) is closed in X.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mWait, I need Ann(M_i) to be finitely generated for V(Ann(M_i)) to make sense as [0m[38;2;124;124;124ma closed subscheme, but V(I) for any ideal I is closed. Ann(M_i) is an ideal [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(finitely generated since A_i is noetherian). V(Ann(M_i)) is closed. Good.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo the statement is true.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me also double check the claim that coherent sheaf on noetherian scheme [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mgives finitely generated module. On a noetherian scheme, coherent = finite type.[0m[38;2;124;124;124mOn affine noetherian Spec A, finite type sheaf corresponds to finitely generated[0m[38;2;124;124;124mA-module. Yes.[0m

